From 69db9580011802f567f2d2181db1e25a64df4c6e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: djrobson5 <djrobson5@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 01:00:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 16/17] Metal: occlusion queries

Implements patch 0005's interface on Metal: createOcclusionQueryPool,
beginQuery/endQuery and getRawResults.

A pool is a shared visibility result buffer cut into 8-byte segments.
Metal counts per render encoder, so a query gets a segment in every
encoder it spans (plume ends encoders on barriers and framebuffer
changes) and getRawResults sums them. The pool's buffer is the
visibility result buffer of every render encoder begun after
resetQueryPool or beginQuery; a query begun in an encoder without it
ends that encoder. Counting mode (sample counts, as Vulkan's precise
queries). Quad clears pause counting (Vulkan's clears are not counted).
Segment 0 belongs to no query: an encoder writes its count to the
current offset when it ends, also with counting off (offset 0), and that
zeroed the first query's count in the self-test.
Results are available once the last command buffer that counted into
the pool completed. resetQueryPool zeroes the segments on the CPU, so
the pool's earlier command buffers must have completed (it waits for
them otherwise). One query counts at a time, as in Vulkan.
